# E327 draft: legacy Bash test harness setup failures must not become false green

id:                     E363
trigger_tool:           bash|conan|test-runner|make|xargs
phase:                  testing
error_signature:        cp: /tmp/.*Read-only file system|/bin/bash: bad interpreter|xargs: Unknown option 'I'|install: Permission denied|ASLTS.*PASS\s*:\s*$|iasl compiler not found.*exit_code=0

severity:               3
category:               ohos, portability, shell, false-green, testing-infrastructure
match_keywords:         read-only /tmp, bare exit, exit code 0, empty Summary, /bin/bash, xargs -I, TMPDIR, positive completion marker
title:                  Legacy Bash test harness setup failures must not be reported as a passing upstream suite

root_cause:             Legacy upstream Bash harnesses can combine three independent portability assumptions: staging executable tools under hard-coded /tmp, executing transitive helpers through a fixed /bin/bash shebang, and using GNU-only utility flags such as xargs -I. If setup and phase errors use bare exit or are not returned to the top-level process, the harness can exit 0 with no test case executed and an empty PASS/FAIL/Tests summary.
affected_scope:         Upstream shell test suites on OHOS or other restricted/POSIX environments that stage tools in a global temporary directory, invoke nested Bash scripts by shebang, parallelize with implementation-specific xargs flags, or judge success only from the top-level exit code.
verification_cmd:       TMPDIR="$PWD/.test-tmp" ASLTS_SKIP_TEMPLATE=yes ASLTS_SKIP_RESULT_COMPARE=yes bash ./aslts.sh -e -u -c constant -m n64 && grep -A12 '^TOTAL:' tests/aslts/tmp/RESULTS/*/Summary

rec_priority:           1
rec_approach:           writable-temp-explicit-interpreter-fail-fast-positive-summary
rec_description:        Honor caller-owned TMPDIR and verify it is writable; declare Bash as a reproducible tool dependency; invoke the top-level and transitive scripts through that Bash instead of a system shebang; use mkdir for pure directory creation instead of a policy-blocked install program; replace unsupported parallel dispatch with a portable selected-case loop; return every setup/compile/execute failure explicitly; and require a non-empty structured summary plus a generated artifact before declaring success.
rec_command:            conan create archives/a/acpica-unix/20260408 --build=missing
rec_auto_fix:           false
rec_impl:               conan-test-asset-patch-and-summary-gate

fallback_priority:      2
fallback_approach:      evidence-bounded-subset
fallback_description:   If an unrelated upstream phase is not portable, expose an explicit opt-in skip for that phase, run a named deterministic subset, retain independent consumer coverage, and report the exact inventory and selection without claiming the full suite.
fallback_command:       ASLTS_SKIP_TEMPLATE=yes bash ./aslts.sh -e -u -c constant -m n64
fallback_auto_fix:      false
fallback_impl:          upstream-runner-environment-switch

forbid_1_pattern:       exit 0.*(iasl compiler not found|bad interpreter|Unknown option)|runner.*exit_code=0.*pass
forbid_1_reason:        A top-level zero code is insufficient when preparation or transitive dispatch failed before any test produced a result.
forbid_1_consequence:   CI records a false upstream-test pass while PASS, FAIL, and Tests are empty.
forbid_2_pattern:       ln -s.*(/bin/bash|/usr/bin/env)|mount.*rw.*(/tmp|/bin)
forbid_2_reason:        A package adaptation must not mutate the device system image to satisfy an upstream test harness.
forbid_2_consequence:   The result is non-reproducible, violates isolation, and may affect other queued jobs.
forbid_3_pattern:       full.*suite.*pass|1291/1291|100%.*ASLTS
forbid_3_reason:        Running one named collection and mode is not execution of every ASL source or every ASLTS mode.
forbid_3_consequence:   Test coverage is overstated and the B-class evidence is not auditable.

principles:             P014

causes:                 []
caused_by:              [E002, E201]
similar_to:             [E253]
conflicts_with:         []
prerequisite_of:        []

